    "content": "Lt. Gen. Sam Okiding, the Deputy Chief of the Uganda People's Defence Forces, arrived in Mogadishu on Monday to attend a meeting of senior military commanders from the African Union Support and Stabilization Mission in Somalia (AUSSOM). His visit underscores Uganda's continued military engagement in Somalia, where it has contributed troops under successive AU missions since 2007.\n\nThe meeting is expected to address operational coordination, security transitions, and the ongoing handover of responsibilities to Somali security forces as part of the broader drawdown plan. Uganda is one of the largest troop contributors to the AU mission, with forces primarily deployed in sectors around Mogadishu and the Lower Shabelle region.\n\nThis gathering comes at a critical time as AUSSOM prepares to assume full mandate from the previous ATMIS mission, with a focus on stabilizing areas recently liberated from militant control and supporting Somali-led security operations. The presence of senior Ugandan leadership signals the mission's commitment to adapting its strategy to current security dynamics.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, particularly those of Ugandan origin or with ties to Uganda, this engagement highlights the strengthened bilateral cooperation between Somalia and Uganda, which has implications for trade, security partnerships, and regional stability. Diaspora communities often follow such military developments closely, as they affect the safety of relatives and investments back home.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/taliyaha-ku-xigeenka-ciidanka-difaaca-uganda-oo-muqdisho-uga-qaybgelaya-shirka-taliyeyaasha-aussom/424477/",
