    "slug": "puntland-launches-2025-2030-justice-strategy-in-garoowe",
    "summary": "Puntland's vice president opened a conference in Garoowe to support the implementation of the region's five-year justice strategy, aiming to strengthen rule of law and access to justice.",
    "content": "GAROOWE, Somalia — Puntland's Vice President Ilyaas Osman Lugatoor officially opened a conference in Garoowe on Tuesday, marking the launch of the implementation and support phase of the Puntland Justice Strategy 2025–2030. The gathering brings together judicial officials, legal experts, and civil society representatives to discuss ways to advance the region's legal framework and improve service delivery.\n\nThe strategy, developed with input from multiple stakeholders, focuses on enhancing the independence and efficiency of the judiciary, expanding legal aid services, and integrating traditional justice mechanisms with formal courts. The opening session highlighted the need for coordinated efforts to address challenges such as case backlogs, limited infrastructure, and shortages of trained judicial personnel.\n\nVice President Lugatoor emphasized the regional government's commitment to ensuring justice is accessible to all citizens, particularly those in remote areas who have historically faced barriers in seeking legal recourse. He called on partners and diaspora communities to contribute to the initiative's success. The conference is expected to produce an action plan for the first year of implementation.\n\nThe initiative comes amid ongoing efforts by Puntland authorities to strengthen governance and rule of law, which are seen as crucial for stability and investment in the region. For the Somali diaspora, this development holds particular relevance as many have family in Puntland and have advocated for legal reforms to protect property rights, resolve disputes, and uphold human rights. The strategy's success could enhance confidence in the region's institutions and encourage diaspora engagement in economic and social development.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/shir-looga-arrinsanayo-caddaaladda-puntland-oo-garoowe-ka-furmay/424461/",
