    "original_title": "Ra&#8217;iisul Wasaare ku-xigeenka Somalia oo iska celinaya dhalashada dalka Kenya.",
    "slug": "somali-deputy-prime-minister-renounces-kenyan-citizenship",
    "summary": "Jabriil Cabdirashiid Xaaji, Somalia’s Deputy Prime Minister, has announced he is renouncing his Kenyan citizenship to align with his role in the federal government.",
    "content": "Mogadishu, Somalia — Somalia’s Second Deputy Prime Minister, Jabriil Cabdirashiid Xaaji, has publicly declared that he is renouncing his Kenyan citizenship. The announcement was made during a press conference in the capital, where he cited the need to fully commit to his duties in the Somali federal government.\n\nBorn in Somalia, Xaaji had acquired Kenyan nationality during his time in exile, a common path for many Somalis who fled the country’s decades of conflict. His decision to relinquish Kenyan citizenship comes after his appointment to the deputy prime minister’s post, a role that requires undivided allegiance to the Somali state.\n\nThe move is legally significant, as Somali law generally prohibits dual citizenship for high-ranking officials, mandating that they hold only Somali nationality. By renouncing his Kenyan passport, Xaaji aims to comply with these constitutional requirements and set an example for other officials who may hold foreign citizenships.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development underscores the complex ties between Somalis abroad and their homeland. Many diaspora members, including politicians, maintain dual citizenship as a safety net, but this case highlights the legal and political pressures they face when taking up senior government positions. Xaaji’s action may encourage others in similar positions to regularize their status, reinforcing the importance of national loyalty in public service.\n\nAs Somalia continues to rebuild its institutions, such gestures are seen as steps toward strengthening governance and constitutional adherence. The government has not yet issued an official statement on the procedure for renunciation, but Xaaji’s announcement marks a clear personal commitment to his office.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/raiisul-wasaare-ku-xigeenka-somalia-oo-iscelinaya-dhalashada-dalka-kenya/424457/",
